# =============================================================================
# eona-x-connector-kit
# =============================================================================
# Nothing in this repository should ever contain a credential. The entries
# below are the ones that would otherwise pick one up by accident.

# --- your own configuration and everything derived from it -------------------
# Un-anchored on purpose: the kit's idiom is "copy .env.example to .env", and
# a .env dropped at the repository root — or next to the scripts — is the
# obvious near-miss. Anchoring these to compose/ would let exactly that
# through.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
# Written by scripts/bootstrap.sh: the participant private key, the public key,
# the management API key and the generated DID document.
compose/secrets/
# Per-service overrides appended verbatim to config.properties.
compose/config/*/extra.properties

# --- key material and certificates -------------------------------------------
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.csr
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.truststore

# --- Helm ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Packaged charts and vendored dependencies.
*.tgz
charts/**/charts/
charts/**/Chart.lock
# Local value overrides. Keep the committed values-*.yaml examples.
values-local*.yaml
*.local.yaml
*.secret.yaml

# --- Kubernetes ---------------------------------------------------------------
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig
.kube/

# --- HashiCorp Vault ----------------------------------------------------------
# Unseal keys and root tokens printed by `vault operator init`.
vault-init.json
unseal-keys*

# --- scratch ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.bak
*.orig
*.tmp
tmp/
out/

# --- editors and OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
